  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "Define positive semidefinite real polynomials and k-square sum representations, prove elementary SOS closure facts, compute Pfister bounds for small dimensions, and formalize the Brahmagupta-Fibonacci identity as the product law for two-square sums.",
    "plain": "Backfill the Hilbert 17 OQ-01 metadata around the verified univariate/SOS scaffold: PSD and SOS definitions, examples like x^2 and x^2+1, monotonicity in the number of squares, Pfister bound values, and the two-square product identity.",
    "whyMatters": [
      "Hilbert's 17th problem asks when nonnegative polynomials are sums of squares of rational functions; this file captures a small verified polynomial-SOS toolkit.",
      "The Brahmagupta-Fibonacci identity is the algebraic engine behind closure of sums of two squares.",
      "The OQ-01 file is zero-axiom and zero-sorry, while the broader Hilbert 17 development still contains deeper axiomatized results."
    ]
  },
  "knownResults": {
    "proven": [
      "`IsPSD`, `IsSumOfKSquares`, and `IsSOS` define the core positivity and sum-of-squares predicates.",
      "`const_nonneg_is_one_square`, `sq_is_psd`, `sq_is_one_square`, `sq_plus_one_psd`, and `sq_plus_one_is_two_squares` provide concrete polynomial examples.",
      "`psd_add`, `sum_of_k_squares_is_psd`, `sum_of_k_squares_mono`, and `sum_of_squares_le` prove basic SOS/PSD closure and monotonicity.",
      "`pfister_bound_mono`, `pfister_univariate`, `pfister_bivariate`, `pfister_trivariate`, `brahmagupta_fibonacci`, `brahmagupta_fibonacci_poly`, `sos2_mul`, and `product_example` record the Pfister-bound and two-square product infrastructure."
    ],
